{# THE CATALOGUE — every module this installation can run, and who runs it.

   THE SAME TABLE THE INSTALLATION SCREEN DRAWS, and deliberately the same:
   one screen asks "what runs where" and this one asks "what is the
   catalogue", and they are the same fact. Two readings of it would be two
   answers with no way to say which was right.

   DRAWN TO ITS SCOPE, NOT TO ITS FULL DEPTH (ruled 2026-09-20). What it
   STATES is settled — the catalogue and the areas that run it. Installing and
   removing a module at organization scope, and the consequence screen that
   says what data an uninstall would orphan, are queued and are not here; the
   hint at the bottom says so rather than leaving a reader to wonder whether
   the buttons are missing or the feature is. #}
{% extends '@Shell/settings/_section.html.twig' %}

{% block shell_page %}
    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">The catalogue<span class="src">&middot;
            {{ settings.matrix.columns|length }} installed &middot;
            running in {{ settings.matrix.liveAreas }} of {{ settings.matrix.rows|length }}
            area{{ settings.matrix.rows|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</span></span>
        <a class="more" href="{{ installationUrl }}">Installation &rarr;</a>
        {{ include('@Shell/settings/_matrix.html.twig', {matrix: settings.matrix}, with_context: false) }}
    </div>

    {{ include('@Shell/_page_hint.html.twig', {
        lead: 'This tab is drawn to its scope, not to its full depth.',
        say: 'What it states is settled: the catalogue, and the areas that run each of them — the matrix above is the reading of it. Still to draw: installing and removing at organization scope, and the screen that says what data an uninstall would orphan.',
    }, with_context: false) }}
{% endblock %}
